WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.410 --> 00:00:05.707
According to the World
Health Organization,

2
00:00:05.790 --> 00:00:07.997
mental health is a state of well-being

3
00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:10.827
in which a person recognises
their own abilities,

4
00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:12.787
can cope with the challenges of life,

5
00:00:12.870 --> 00:00:16.022
work productively and contribute
to their community.

6
00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:20.557
Well-being can be described
as the perception of emotional balance,

7
00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:23.667
life satisfaction and a sense of purpose.

8
00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:27.217
At work, it means the experience
of feeling valued,

9
00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:31.865
safe, competent and in balance
with the different areas of life.

10
00:00:32.630 --> 00:00:37.218
It should be stressed that mental health
and well-being are not static states.

11
00:00:37.510 --> 00:00:40.507
They vary over time
and depending on the context.

12
00:00:40.590 --> 00:00:43.037
Work, as a central part of daily life,

13
00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:45.927
has a direct impact on this variation.

14
00:00:46.130 --> 00:00:49.707
Thinking about mental health
therefore necessarily means

15
00:00:49.790 --> 00:00:51.957
considering the context the person is in,

16
00:00:52.040 --> 00:00:55.697
including working conditions,
interpersonal relationships,

17
00:00:55.780 --> 00:01:00.127
the organisation of tasks
and the organisational culture.

18
00:01:00.210 --> 00:01:03.427
Recognising this interdependence
is an essential step

19
00:01:03.510 --> 00:01:07.113
towards creating healthier
and more sustainable environments.
